     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section content-section" aria-labelledby="method-heading">
  <h2 id="method-heading">How to Convert GMT to ACST</h2>
  <p class="method-intro">
    Because ACST uses a half-hour offset (UTC+9:30), converting GMT to ACST requires adding 9 full hours and then adding an additional 30 minutes.
  </p>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <div class="method-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Method 1</p>
      <h3>Two-Step Addition Rule</h3>
      <p>
        Add 9 hours to the GMT time, then add 30 minutes. Example: 8:00 AM GMT plus 9 hours = 5:00 PM, plus 30 minutes = 5:30 PM ACST on the same day.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="method-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Method 2</p>
      <h3>Next Day Calendar Rollover Rule</h3>
      <p>
        Any GMT timestamp after 2:30 PM GMT rolls over into the next calendar day in Central Australia (e.g. 5:00 PM GMT Tuesday = 2:30 AM ACST Wednesday).
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="method-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Method 3</p>
